  "worked_solution": "The multiples of $2$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nS={2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nT={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nNow, $T\u2216S$ is the *difference* of $T$ and $S,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $T$ but *not* in $S.$\n\nThe elements of $T$ that are also in $S$ are $4,8,12,16,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $4$). So, we must remove these elements from $T.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\u2216S & ={4,8,12,16,\u2026}-{2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,\u2026} \\\\  & =\u2205.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
